# ─── Configuration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env and .runner.env are deliberately TRACKED: this repository is private and
# the team wants deployments to carry their configuration.
#
# They hold the JWT secret, webhook secret, database URI, the DeepSeek API key,
# the n8n encryption key (which decrypts every stored n8n credential) and the
# Postgres password. Two consequences worth knowing:
#   - anyone with read access to the repo has all of them;
#   - git keeps them in history forever, so rotating a key later does not remove
#     the old one from earlier commits.
# If the repo is ever made public, treat every value in these files as leaked.
*.pem
*.key

# ─── WhatsApp session state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Baileys auth material. Anyone holding these can send messages as the linked
# account.
sessions/
whatsapp-api/sessions/
auth/

# ─── Customer data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Received media is customer documents: birth certificates, NIDs, e-TINs.
# Never publish these.
whatsapp-api/public/received_media/
received_media/
*.sqlite
dump/
backups/

# Real vendor phone numbers (personal data). Ship vendors.example.txt instead.
vendors.txt
!vendors.example.txt

# ─── Dependencies and build output ────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
/build
/coverage

# Python virtualenv and downloaded Whisper models
.venv-voice/
.models/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ─── Local / editor noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
.trae/
.env
n8n/.env
*.env